==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|resuscitatus}}, past participle of {{m|la|resuscitare||to raise up again, revive}}, from {{m|la|re-||again}} + {{m|la|suscitare||to raise up}}, from {{m|la|sub-||up, under}} + {{m|la|citare||to summon, rouse}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈsʌsɪˌteɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-resuscitate.wav|Audio (RP)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[restore]] [[consciousness]], [[vigor]], or [[life]] to.
#: ''to '''resuscitate''' a drowned person; to '''resuscitate''' withered plants''
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[regain]] [[consciousness]].

====Synonyms====
*{{sense|to regain consciousness}} {{l|en|come to}}

